# Fixes from two reviews of the guide's Keep it safe step, one of its behavior and one of its texts, for the page's next
# image (1.1.0, not published). On an Apple Silicon Mac, Docker Desktop, no umbrelOS, no cost. The page from this
# checkout; relay 0.3.0's image and the package's other images as pinned. The mocked suites, the browser test and the
# previews on ports 8801 to 8808 only, then check.py on a fresh up.sh run with the page on 8809, removed afterwards with
# down.sh, then Umbrel's linter and the screenshots.

# What changed, by the reviews' items:
# 1. Back after Moderation's link to the step: the link added an entry to the history, so Back fired hashchange for the
#    step the address named before (#phone, from the guide's own links), opened it and scrolled away from Settings, and
#    with the address at #safe already the link fired nothing and focus fell to the page. The script now handles every
#    link to a step as the guide's own links: the address replaced, the step at its first drawing, in view, focus on its
#    heading. hashchange stays for a step's name typed into the address bar. Back after the link now leaves the page.
# 2. On a phone the stepper moved between the step's two drawings, 45 to 217 pixels from 320 to 540 wide, since the tall
#    drawing grew to 1.27 times its size. It stops at 360 pixels wide; under 480 pixels of drawing width both drawings
#    get one height, the tall one's with its labels and room for other fonts, and at least 360; the wide drawing's range
#    gets at least 306, where the lists were 8 pixels taller. The stepper's count, title and buttons line up on the
#    title's first line, so a title that wraps to more lines doesn't move the buttons: that alone moved them 12 pixels
#    at 375, and the first step's 2 to 12 pixels from 320 to 390. Measured from 320 to 1440 pixels, no step's buttons
#    move between its two drawings now; on a computer the drawings stay 340 pixels tall.
# 3. The open community's two lists and the three notes say role="list": Safari drops the role from a list drawn
#    without bullets.
# 4. The tall drawing's labels are the page's text under it, at its scale, as the wide one's are, so with WCAG 1.4.12's
#    text spacing they wrap instead of running into each other. The drawing stops at 311 of the guide's 348.
# 5 to 7. The texts, below. 8. The dead rule .next + details.alt is gone. 9. The drawing's description goes into
#    aria-label through esc(): its apostrophe is escaped, and a screen reader hears the same.
# 10. render.py has its own copy of that description, checks the words drawn in each drawing and their labels, and
#    that the live page loads nothing from another host: no src= naming one, no stylesheet or @import, every url() a
#    #id, and every href in its SVGs a #id or the agent's picture as data:image/webp.
# 11. The drawings' rules ship only with the live page: 7,064 bytes less on every other page (domain-dns 65,827 to
#    58,763, setup 76,631 to 69,567); the live page 172,518 to 173,575 (domain-live), with the labels and roles.

# The texts that changed, before and after:
# - Private channels, while Moderation is on:
#   "While Moderation is on, you and staff you add can open any message stored here by its ID, deleted ones included,
#   even in private channels and direct messages."
#   "While Moderation is on, the owner and the staff they add can open any message stored here by its ID, deleted ones
#   included, even in private channels and direct messages."
# - Settings, Moderation, on a live page:
#   "Members don't see this in Buzz. The Keep it safe step above says it, so share it."
#   "Members don't see this in Buzz, so tell them. While Moderation is on, the Private channels note in Keep it safe
#   above says it." (Keep it safe a link to the step)
# - Settings, Moderation, while connecting:
#   "Members don't see this in Buzz. Once your community is live, the Keep it safe step on this page says it, so share it."
#   "Members don't see this in Buzz, so tell them. Once your community is live, the Private channels note in the Keep it
#   safe step says it while Moderation is on."
# - The tall drawing's reply, under a caption that says not to connect agents to your code:
#   "On it. Working from the app repo." -> "On it.", as on the wide drawing.

$ python3 tests/umbrel/local/render.py
